<document xmlns="http://cnx.rice.edu/cnxml" xmlns:m="http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML">
  <title>7.11.2: The Factored Form of a Quadratic Expression and the <emphasis effect="italics">x</emphasis>-intercepts of Its Graph</title>
  <metadata xmlns:md="http://cnx.rice.edu/mdml">
    <md:content-id>m01924</md:content-id>
    <md:title>7.11.2: The Factored Form of a Quadratic Expression and the X-Intercepts of Its Graph</md:title>
    <md:uuid>d888f675-5c48-481a-bafa-48bdcdd60680</md:uuid>
  </metadata>
  <content>
    <section id="sect-00001">
      <title>Activity</title>
      <para id="para-00001">Consider two functions defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00001">
        <item>Consider the function defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
      </list>
      <para id="para-00002">Then, answer questions a–g, and create a table of values in which to enter the given x values and their outputs using the function.</para>
   
        <exercise id="fbf538bb-f2c6-4352-9d03-9245f6291f4a" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00001">
            
            <para id="para-00003">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00001">
            <para id="para-00004">Correct! 0</para>
            <para id="para-00005">The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_7e3b60e8-2698-4351-b519-0dbf05268d6c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00002">
            
            <para id="para-00006">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00002">
            <para id="para-00007">Correct! -3</para>
            <para id="para-00008">The correct answer is -3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_36eff251-576a-4a08-a292-23ebe6b0caed" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00003">
            
            <para id="para-00009">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00003">
            <para id="para-00010">Correct! 0</para>
            <para id="para-00011">The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="c7ec1749-f6a9-420d-b76f-5177b09b99d9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00004">
            
            <para id="para-00012">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00004">
            <para id="para-00013">Correct! 5</para>
            <para id="para-00014">The correct answer is 5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_4ead2d8e-cb7a-4723-884e-3f093a5cfd92" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00005">
            
            <para id="para-00015">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00005">
            <para id="para-00016">Correct! 12</para>
            <para id="para-00017">The correct answer is 12.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_3e2149b6-ffc9-4aa2-b353-5138c9cac85c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00006">
            
            <para id="para-00018">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00006">
            <para id="para-00019">Correct! 21</para>
            <para id="para-00020">The correct answer is 21.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="d7ee71b0-6b6c-47ba-9a7a-331832b8b0b4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00007">
            
            <para id="para-00021">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00007">
            <para id="para-00022">Correct! 45</para>
            <para id="para-00023">The correct answer is 45.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>

      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00002">
        <item>Now, answer questions a–d to analyze the function defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>+</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00001">
        <problem id="prob-00008">
          <para id="para-00024">What are the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00008">
          <para id="para-00025">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00026">The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts for function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. These points have an <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate that makes the output value 0.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section id="sect-00003">
        <exercise id="cd4fd094-81f0-44ce-bdc2-7c8ffd4a284c" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00009">
            
            <para id="para-00027">What is the value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate in the vertex of the graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00009">
            <para id="para-00028">Correct! -2</para>
            <para id="para-00029">The correct answer is -2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="efc5a9b1-58bb-48f7-afa5-e4c45538c19e" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00010">
            
            <para id="para-00030">What is the value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate in the vertex of the graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00010">
            <para id="para-00031">Correct! -4</para>
            <para id="para-00032">The correct answer is -4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00002">
        <problem id="prob-00011">
          <para id="para-00033">What is the vertex of the graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00011">
          <para id="para-00034">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00035">The vertex appears to be at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. From the tables, the function values seem to change from decreasing to increasing at those points.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00003">
        <item>Consider the function defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.
    
    Then, answer questions a–g, and create a table of values in which to enter the given x values and their outputs using the function.
 </item>
      </list>
      <section  id="sect-00004">
        <exercise id="e2b10c58-e3be-4468-b659-41230961de8d" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00012">
            
            <para id="para-00036">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00012">
            <para id="para-00037">Correct! 32</para>
            <para id="para-00038">The correct answer is 32.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_0ded0a1a-af60-483d-8d79-07df7ca15ea9" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00013">
            
            <para id="para-00039">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00013">
            <para id="para-00040">Correct! 21</para>
            <para id="para-00041">The correct answer is 21.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_22c89b68-2f83-45e6-9397-cb6cccd55df5" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00014">
            
            <para id="para-00042">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00014">
            <para id="para-00043">Correct! 0</para>
            <para id="para-00044">The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="fc365c44-9ee1-4f0b-b7f9-4e1165326aad" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00015">
            
            <para id="para-00045">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00015">
            <para id="para-00046">Correct! -3</para>
            <para id="para-00047">The correct answer is -3.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="dcbf8f49-f691-4ee2-b84d-5e96b1cfd5d4" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00016">
            
            <para id="para-00048">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00016">
            <para id="para-00049">Correct! -4</para>
            <para id="para-00050">The correct answer is -4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_570ad872-751f-4c87-b55b-f71032c93d75" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00017">
            
            <para id="para-00051">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00017">
            <para id="para-00052">Correct! 0</para>
            <para id="para-00053">The correct answer is 0.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_5b0b1aff-8af2-4e7b-9fdc-0c41da2f0930" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00018">
            
            <para id="para-00054">When the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>, what is the value of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00018">
            <para id="para-00055">Correct! 5</para>
            <para id="para-00056">The correct answer is 5.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00004">
        <item>Now, answer questions a–d to analyze the function defined by <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
      </list>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00003">
        <problem id="prob-00019">
          <para id="para-00057">What are the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts of the graph? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00019">
          <para id="para-00058">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00059">The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts for function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> are <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. These points have an <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate that makes the output value 0.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <section id="sect-00005">
        <exercise id="_3192dc06-76cb-40d2-9e9b-1ead9c311094" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00020">
            
            <para id="para-00060">What is the value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate in the vertex of the graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00020">
            <para id="para-00061">Correct! 2</para>
            <para id="para-00062">The correct answer is 2.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
        <exercise id="_94ee4a87-d64f-4f3a-ad32-31ba6177aa8b" class="multiple-choice">
          <problem id="prob-00021">
            
            <para id="para-00063">What is the value of the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate in the vertex of the graph?</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00021">
            <para id="para-00064">Correct! -4</para>
            <para id="para-00065">The correct answer is -4.</para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      </section>
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00004">
        <problem id="prob-00022">
          <para id="para-00066">What is the vertex of the graph of function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>g</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>? Be prepared to show your reasoning.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00022">
          <para id="para-00067">Compare your answer:</para>
          <para id="para-00068">The vertex appears to be at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>4</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>. From the tables, the function values seem to change from decreasing to increasing at those points.</para>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
      <media alt=""><iframe src="../../media/desmos/a47b5bb4ba783be55a7067b919f165f14dcc36ce.html" width="500" height="400"/></media>
        
        <list class="os-raise-noindent" list-type="enumerated" id="list-00005">
        <item>Use the graphing tool or technology outside the course.</item>
      </list>
      
        <exercise id="exer-00005">
          <problem id="prob-00023">
            <para id="para-00069">Plot the points from the tables on the same coordinate plane. (Consider using different colors or markings for each set of points so you can tell them apart.)</para>
            <para id="para-00070">Select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          </problem>
          <solution id="sol-00023">
            <para id="para-00071">Compare your answer:</para>
            <para id="para-00072">
                      <media alt="Coordinate grid with two graphs shown by plotted points.">
                  <image mime-type="image/svg+xml" src="../../media/Algebra-1_08_13_03_01.svg"/>
                </media>
              
          </para>
          </solution>
        </exercise>
      
      <!--Text Entry Interaction Start -->
      <exercise id="exer-00006">
        <problem id="prob-00024">
          <para id="para-00073">Make a couple of observations about how the two graphs compare.</para>
          
        </problem>
        <solution id="sol-00024">
          <para id="para-00074">Compare your answer:</para>
          <list id="list-00006">
            <item>The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercept of both graphs is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</item>
            <item>The graphs seem to be a reflection of each other across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis.</item>
            <item>The vertices both have a <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-coordinate of -4 and also mirror one another across the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-axis.</item>
            <item>Each function mirrors itself across a vertical line through its vertex.</item>
          </list>
        </solution>
      </exercise>
      <!--Interaction End -->
    </section>

    <note class="self-check" id="note-00001"><para id="para-00075">The table for function <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math> is below. What is the vertex of the graph of <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>?</para>
      <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00003">
        <tgroup cols="7"><tbody><row>
            <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis> </entry><entry> -3 </entry>
            <entry> -2 </entry>
            <entry> -1 </entry>
            <entry> 0 </entry>
            <entry> 1 </entry>
            <entry> 2 </entry>
          </row>
          <row>
            <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis> </entry><entry> 0 </entry>
            <entry> -1 </entry>
            <entry> -3 </entry>
            <entry> -1 </entry>
            <entry> 0 </entry>
            <entry> 2 </entry>
          </row>
        </tbody></tgroup></table>
      </note>

      <section id="sect-00006"><title>Determining Parts of a Graph from a Table</title>
        <para id="para-00076">Identify the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts and vertex of the quadratic from the table:</para>
        <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00001">
          <tgroup cols="6"><tbody><row>
              <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry><entry>
                <para id="para-00077">-5</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00078">-3</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00079">-1</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00080">0</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00081">1</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
            <row>
              <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry><entry>
                <para id="para-00082">16</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00083">0</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00084">-2</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00085">0</para>
              </entry>
              <entry>
                <para id="para-00086">16</para>
              </entry>
            </row>
          </tbody></tgroup></table>
        
        <para id="para-00087">The <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-intercepts are where the <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>y</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math>-values are 0.</para>
        <para id="para-00088">This occurs at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>3</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <para id="para-00089">The vertex occurs where the function will create a mirror image, or be symmetrical for all points. This often occurs halfway between the two zeros (when there are two zeros).</para>
        <para id="para-00090">For this function, the vertex is at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>1</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mo>−</m:mo><m:mn>2</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
        <note class="try" id="note-00002">
        <title> Try It: Determining Parts of a Graph from a Table </title>
        <exercise id="exer-00007">
          <problem id="prob-00025">
            
            <para id="para-00091">Determine the vertex from the table:</para>
            
            <table class="os-raise-horizontaltable" id="table-00002">
              <tgroup cols="7"><tbody><row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry><entry>
                    <para id="para-00092">5</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00093">6</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00094">7</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00095">8</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00096">9</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00097">10</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
                <row>
                  <entry><emphasis><m:math><m:mrow><m:mi>f</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math></emphasis></entry><entry>
                    <para id="para-00098">0</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00099">4</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00100">8</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00101">4</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00102">0</para>
                  </entry>
                  <entry>
                    <para id="para-00103">-2</para>
                  </entry>
                </row>
              </tbody></tgroup></table>
            
            
          
          <para id="para-00104">Write down your answer, then select the <emphasis>solution</emphasis> button to compare your work.</para>
          
          </problem><solution id="sol-00025">
          <para id="para-00105">Here is how to determine the vertex from the table:</para>
          
          <para id="para-00106">The zeros are located at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>5</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math> and <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>9</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>0</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.
            The vertex will be halfway between the two zeros. This occurs at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          
          <para id="para-00107">The point in the table at <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mi>x</m:mi><m:mo>=</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn></m:mrow></m:math> is <m:math display="inline"><m:mrow><m:mo stretchy="false">(</m:mo><m:mn>7</m:mn><m:mo>,</m:mo><m:mn>8</m:mn><m:mo stretchy="false">)</m:mo></m:mrow></m:math>.</para>
          
          <para id="para-00108">This is the vertex.</para>
        
        </solution></exercise></note>
        </section>
  </content>
</document>
